{
  "about": "VG-CLI-OPTIONS: one command line per case, run in all three engines; each must give the expected exit code and refusal key, and a refused run writes nothing under --out. --json goes right after the first token unless 'json' says front (first) or none (left out). Each run starts in a fresh empty working directory: {root} expands to the repository root, {B} to the quickstart bundle and profile, {out} to <cwd>/out. Optional: 'writes' names the one entry the run leaves in its working directory (null: none); 'says' (one token or a list) must appear on stdout or stderr; 'same_stdout' requires byte-identical stdout across engines; 'debug_log' names the command Python's command.start and command.end records on stderr must carry; 'envelope' names the command whose successful --json envelope stdout must be; 'has' names a path (or a list of paths) the run must write, 'first_line' a file's required first line and 'file_says' a file and a token it must hold, all judged only in engines without an override. 'engines' overrides the expectation for named engines, with the reason; every override names the item that removes it.",
